{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/course_hotsite_link

    A course's enrolment hotsite from the course settings form: its public
    address, shown as text so that it can be read out or copied, a button that
    copies it, and a link opening the page.

    Rendered into a static form element, so it carries no form control of its
    own: the address is a code element, not an input, and never travels with
    the form. The copy button follows core's copy_to_clipboard contract (the
    data-action and data-clipboard-target attributes) and the module is
    required at the end. When the site's router is not configured the address
    is the page's long one and a sentence below says why.

    A course whose guest access needs no password gets a second row of the same
    shape: the guest entry's address, which skips the hotsite and opens the
    course as a guest, with its own copy button and link; on a course that is
    not public a sentence says the address takes in logged-in readers only.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * url - Address of the course's enrolment hotsite: the short public one, or the page's own.
    * addressid - Id of the element holding the address, the copy button's target.
    * addresslabel - Visible label of the address.
    * copylabel - Text of the copy button.
    * copied - Message shown once the address has been copied.
    * label - Visible text of the link.
    * newwindow - Announcement that the link opens a new window, for screen readers only.
    * note - Sentence explaining that the page shows the saved state.
    * routeroff - Sentence shown when the site's router is not configured; empty otherwise.
    * guest - The guest entry's row, or null when the course does not offer it:
      * url - The guest entry's address: its own short one, or the page's with guest=1.
      * addressid - Id of the element holding the address, the copy button's target.
      * addresslabel - Visible label of the address.
      * addresssub - Short line under the label saying what the address does.
      * label - Visible text of the link.
      * notpublic - Sentence shown when the course is not public; empty otherwise.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "url": "https://example.org/p/batepo",
        "addressid": "theme_dimensions-hotsiteaddress-2",
        "addresslabel": "Public address",
        "copylabel": "Copy address",
        "copied": "Address copied",
        "label": "View the enrolment hotsite",
        "newwindow": "(Opens in new window)",
        "note": "This is the public address to share. It opens the enrolment hotsite as it is saved right now, so save your changes first to see them there.",
        "routeroff": "",
        "guest": {
            "url": "https://example.org/p/kabutu",
            "addressid": "theme_dimensions-hotsiteguestaddress-2",
            "addresslabel": "Enter as guest",
            "addresssub": "Skips the hotsite",
            "label": "Open the course as a guest",
            "notpublic": ""
        }
    }
}}
<div class="dimensions-hotsitelink">
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-2 mb-2">
        <span class="fw-bold">{{addresslabel}}</span>
        <code id="{{addressid}}" class="text-break">{{url}}</code>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" data-action="copytoclipboard"
                data-clipboard-target="#{{addressid}}" data-clipboard-success-message="{{copied}}">{{copylabel}}</button>
    </div>
    <a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="{{url}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        {{label}}<span class="visually-hidden"> {{newwindow}}</span>
    </a>
    <div class="form-text">{{note}}</div>
    {{#routeroff}}
    <div class="form-text">{{routeroff}}</div>
    {{/routeroff}}
    {{#guest}}
    <div class="dimensions-hotsitelink__guest mt-3">
        <div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-2 mb-2">
            <span class="fw-bold">{{addresslabel}} <span class="fw-normal text-muted">· {{addresssub}}</span></span>
            <code id="{{addressid}}" class="text-break">{{url}}</code>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" data-action="copytoclipboard"
                    data-clipboard-target="#{{addressid}}" data-clipboard-success-message="{{copied}}">{{copylabel}}</button>
        </div>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="{{url}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            {{label}}<span class="visually-hidden"> {{newwindow}}</span>
        </a>
        {{#notpublic}}
        <div class="form-text">{{notpublic}}</div>
        {{/notpublic}}
    </div>
    {{/guest}}
</div>
{{#js}}
require(['core/copy_to_clipboard']);
{{/js}}
